=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_c4f9 — Kitchen utensils live at the sink; the pot lives in the pantry

The shared cooking implements in this house — cutting board, kitchen knife, pan, and spatula — are stored at the sink area, not on the counter and not carried around. They are washed and put back at the sink after use, and that is where the robot finds them the vast majority of the time. The pot, by contrast, lives on the pantry shelf. The snack bowl is a counter item (it holds snacks for grazing) and stays at the kitchen counter. None of these items travel out of the house; they are fixed kitchen fixtures.

What sets this apart: the mixture's statistical model was predicting several of these items as ON_PERSON (likely because a resident was briefly seen near the kitchen), but the sightings show them consistently at sink_k1. p_a3f7 and other documents do not address these shared utensils at all. This document pins them to specific receptacles so the robot stops looking for them on a resident's person.

What would refute it: finding the cutting board, knife, pan, or spatula on the counter, at the dining table, or ON_PERSON on more than one occasion; or finding the pot at the sink rather than the pantry shelf.

